00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,120
I understand.

121
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,240
I understand.

122
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:45,720
Uh lasers are made.

123
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:50,280
Well, there's a lot of different lasers, and it would take a long time to go through all the different types of lasers that there are.

124
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:56,520
It's a long question uh long answer to a short question uh to go into that.

125
00:12:56,520 --> 00:13:03,080
Uh the most popular lasers, I'll tell you this, uh, are uh helium neon lasers used for holography.

126
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:06,760
Most of your amateur and hobbyist philographers are using helium neon lasers.

127
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:12,920
They're very inexpensive, they have a long life, uh, 20,000 hours plus.

128
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:28,680
And um they're basically a glass tube that is uh about the size of a drinking straw, the actual uh place where the lasing action takes place, and that glass tube is filled with the mixtures of the gases, helium and neon.

129
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:36,440
It's the same helium that you find in the helium birthday balloons, it's the same neon that you find in the neon pizza signs when you go out at night to pick up a pizza.

130
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:43,800
And just like a pizza sign, when you apply power to that tube, that tube lights up just like the pizza sign does.

131
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:54,200
Now, even though most of the light's escaping through the sides of the tube, we do have mirrors that are placed on the ends of the tube, and the light begins to reflect back and forth between the two mirrors.

132
00:13:54,200 --> 00:14:08,360
Uh one of the mirrors is uh partially reflective, which means when the light is being reflected back and forth between those two mirrors, this specific mirror allows a certain amount of the light to come through, a certain percentage, and that comes through as the laser beam.

133
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:09,960
Uh, how are holograms made?

134
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:12,520
Well, holograms are made using the laser.

135
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:16,480
There are certain properties of laser light that we need in order to make a hologram.

136
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:22,800
The light needs to be monochromatic, which means it's one color and one color only at a given time.

137
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:33,040
And the light source also has to be coherent, which means all of the waves that are traveling out of that laser are in step with one another in what I like to term wave train.

138
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:40,080
And it are it's these properties of the laser itself and the laser light specifically that allow us to make the holograms.

139
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:49,360
The holograms are made in usually holographic labs, either professional laboratories or amateur studios that you find in some people's basements and even out in garages.

140
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:56,960
There's a holographic table that's usually used, and this holographic table is used to dampen vibrations coming up from the floor.

141
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:03,680
It needs to be a very stiff table so that you don't get a lot of flex, and that laser beam travels around the table.

142
00:15:03,680 --> 00:15:11,440
For a simple hologram, you just need one beam with the object placed behind the plate and spread that laser beam out and cover it with light.

143
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:17,360
More complex holograms, you take that laser beam and break it up into a bunch of different beams using a beam splitter.

144
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:18,640
Send it around the table.

145
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:31,120
You may have one, two, three, or more object beams illuminating your object, and one beam, which is specifically used to illuminate the holographic plate or film, which is called the reference beam.

146
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:34,080
It doesn't have to be a very complex process.

147
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:38,800
It can be very simple, and you don't necessarily have to have a large holographic table.

148
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:47,360
I've made holograms on top of tabletops just using a few simple items in order to make the hologram itself.

149
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:49,840
So David, I hope that answers your question.

